Hadley:

I'm happy to do this in any way that is most useful to you.  But I'm not sure what you mean by a test case, or how it is different than what I put in the first email.  This is the simplest way I could think of to replicate the problem.

If you run the following code:

x <- array(1:(30*5*5), dim=c(30,5,5))
y <- aaply(x, c(1,2), mean)
z1 <- rowMeans(y)
z2 <- aaply(y, 1, mean)

then one should (I think) expect for z1 and z2 to be the same.  They aren't the same; the order is different.  It looks like the output of the second aaply is being ordered as if the numbers 1:30 are characters, not numbers.

I don't do bug reports very often, so if there is some other information that you need to help you replicate the problem, please let me know.  But I did try my best to offer a self-contained, reproducible example.

Michael

