Here a simple 2 step approach

dataset:

MP	H	IDU
1	1	a
1	1	a

1	1	b
1	2	c
2	1	d
2	1	d
2	1	e
2	2	f

tab <- read.delim2("clipboard", header = T, sep = '\t')

#! First summary
summ1 <- ddply(tab, c("MP","H"), summarize, IDU_H =
length(unique(IDU)))

> summ1
  MP H IDU_H
1  1 1     2
2  1 2     1
3  2 1     2
4  2 2     1

#! Second, with summaries for each MP period controlling variation on
H

summ2 <- ddply(summ1, c("MP"), summarize, IDU_H_Mean = mean(IDU_H),
  IDU_H_Max=max(IDU_H),IDU_H_Min = min(IDU_H), IDU_H_SD=sd(IDU_H))

> summ2
  MP IDU_H_Mean IDU_H_Max IDU_H_Min  IDU_H_SD
1  1        1.5         2         1 0.7071068
2  2        1.5         2         1 0.7071068

Is this achievable with a single step ddply() summary?

Paulo

