I am trying to use the name of a string object as the column
on which to summarize. A sample data set is,

structure(list(factor = c("CA01PHF",
"CA02DNS", "CA02DNS", "CA02DNS",

"CA02DNS", "CA02PHF",
"CA03DNS", "CA03DNS", "CA04DNS",
"CA04DNS",

"CA04DNS", "CA04DNS",
"CB01RCA", "CB01RCA"), value = c(0.417714477466949,

0.90595611336548, -0.0912105279735158, 2.35953643919453,
2.42984912516162,

3.01274616561837, -2.62287846202045, -1.04103370735644,
0.997433783115294,

0.292808410166579, -1.67107734452788, 0.747935650795302,
-2.35656465787096,

2.84301978780404)), .Names = c("factor",
"value"), row.names = c(492L,

1212L, 1253L, 1352L, 1392L, 493L, 1213L, 1353L, 1214L,
1254L,

1354L, 1393L, 494L, 1045L), class = "data.frame")

Using this command I get the proper results,

dataMeans <- ddply(data, .(factor), summarise, total =
sum(value))

   factor      total

1 CA01PHF  0.4177145

2 CA02DNS  5.6041311

3 CA02PHF  3.0127462

4 CA03DNS -3.6639122

5 CA04DNS  0.3671005

6 CB01RCA  0.4864551

However if I use a string variable instead to represent the
column name I get either an error or the total sum rather than the sum by
.(factor)

I’ve tried other methods but can’t seem to get it working
properly.

stringName <- "value”

> dataMeans <- ddply(data, .(factor), summarise, total
= sum(stringName))

Error in sum(stringName) : invalid 'type' (character) of
argument

dataMeans <- ddply(data, .(factor), summarise, total =
sum(data[,stringName]))

   factor    total

1 CA01PHF 6.224235

2 CA02DNS 6.224235

3 CA02PHF 6.224235

4 CA03DNS 6.224235

5 CA04DNS 6.224235

6 CB01RCA 6.224235

